The pinned upstream commit is recorded in egm/UPSTREAM.json. Files under egm/
are copied verbatim by scripts/sync-upstream.sh; nothing in that directory is
modified by this project.

The Elephant-Goldfish Model is not an officially supported Google product.
This project is an independent pi adapter. It is not affiliated with,
sponsored by, or endorsed by Google. The names "Elephant-Goldfish Model" and
"EGM" are used descriptively to identify the upstream workflow this adapter
runs. The upstream logo and brand assets are not used here.

Delegation mechanics in extensions/egm.ts (spawning one `pi --mode json`
process per reviewer, parsing JSON session events, and abort handling) follow
the `subagent` example shipped with @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent, which is
MIT licensed:

